  "facts": [
    "Opened on 20 August 1980, the Schöneich Tunnel first stretched roughly 750 m, linking Zurich Schwamendingen to the Letten Tunnel and carving a vital artery through the city’s motorway network.",
    "The 2024 Einhausung Schwamendingen project added a 940 m extension, boosting the tunnel’s length to 1.7 km and cementing its status as one of Zurich’s longest motorway passages.",
    "Beneath the Schöneich Tunnel, tram lines 7 and 9 run in a dedicated tunnel, showcasing a rare blend of road and rail infrastructure beneath the same corridor."
